# Servo on CuBit (docs/servo-port.md): cubitshell renders the pages listed in
# @system/servo/pages with SWGL into memory and reports each frame. Its fonts
# are linked in (the disk has none); the host serves one page over HTTP and
# one over HTTPS (trusted through the test CA installed as the trust store).
(startup v1
  (start "logstore.svc" (priority 5) (test-console approve-declared))
  (start "clock.svc" (priority 5))
  # Services Penny's manifest requires (CAP-003 refuses its launch without
  # them): the desktop session, as in init-servo-desktop.ccl. The batch
  # pages still run (servo/batch-test), in Penny's window.
  (start "display.svc" (priority 5))
  (start "metrics.svc" (priority 2))
  (start "desktop.svc" (priority 4))
  (start "cubitshell.app" (priority 3) (network approve-declared))
)
